		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=3406#p3406"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Umm I was under the impression that an AABB struture was bound to have equal or more nodes than an OBB.</div></blockquote>No, you're right. You're just confused about CD libs. I compared Opcode to Solid, not to Rapid:<br>- Rapid uses OBB trees, and doesn't support deformable meshes<br>- Solid uses AABB trees, and does support them.<br>- Opcode is like Solid, but with less nodes in the trees.<br><br><br>- Pierre<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=76">Pierre</a> — Thu Feb 01, 2007 9:05 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
